## v0.6.7 – Sessions as Single Source of Truth for Timer Duration

**Date:** 2025-12-19 21:30 PST

### Changes Made:
- Refactored frontend timer to calculate duration from sessions array instead of task.duration
- Added `calculateFromSessions()` helper that sums completed session durations + active session elapsed time
- Updated backend to always derive task.duration from sum of session durations
- Fixed GORM `Save()` not persisting session Duration by using explicit `Updates()` calls
- Changed backend duration calculation to use loaded sessions slice (fixes SQLite transaction isolation)
- Backend GetActiveTask now returns all sessions (not just active ones)
- Updated periodic sync (30s) to calculate duration from sessions instead of trusting frontend value
- Updated stopping logic to calculate total from sessions after closing active session
- Fixed column deletion to work for any column (not just last) with proper reordering
- Added test for column deletion with index reordering
- Connected ActionBar "Add new task" button to task creation modal
- Connected ActionBar "Add new column" button to column creation
- Hidden filter button in ActionBar (not connected yet)
- Updated styling for ActionBar dropdown keybind indicators
- Added browser refresh debug logging for timer diagnostics

### Current Status:
- All backend tests passing (handlers, models)
- All frontend tests passing (36 tests)
- Sessions are now the single source of truth for task duration
- Frontend ignores task.duration field, calculates from sessions array
- Backend always calculates task.duration from session durations on save
- Timer values persist correctly across resume/stop cycles

